# Validation & Recovery Diagnosis - Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    %% External Inputs
    Upstash[Upstash Redis <br> Queue: risk-validation]
    
    %% Worker Components
    subgraph Validation Module
        Worker[Validation Worker <br> src/application/validation-worker.ts]
        Guard1{Processing Guard <br> Atomic Claim & Lease}
        Guard2{Initial Resolution Guard <br> Check RevenueObligation}
        Loader[Context Repository <br> Load DB Data]
        
        subgraph Pure Domain Engines
            Diag[Diagnosis Engine <br> Precedence Rules]
            Act[Actionability Engine <br> Math Score]
            Prio[Priority Engine <br> Category Mapping]
            Econ[Economic Engine <br> ERV & NER]
        end
        
        FinalGuard{Final Resolution Guard <br> SELECT FOR UPDATE}
        DBWriter[Result Persistence <br> Prisma $transaction]
    end

    %% Storage
    DB[(Neon PostgreSQL)]
    TableRE[RiskEvent]
    TableRO[RevenueObligation]
    TableVR[ValidationResult]
    TableOB[OutboxEvent]

    %% Flow
    Upstash -- "Consumes Job (Minimal Payload)" --> Worker
    Worker --> Guard1
    Guard1 -- "Updates processingStatus" --> TableRE
    Guard1 --> Guard2
    Guard2 -- "Reads" --> TableRO
    Guard2 -- "If UNRESOLVED" --> Loader
    Loader -- "Fetches Context" --> DB
    Loader --> Diag
    Diag --> Act --> Prio --> Econ
    Econ --> FinalGuard
    FinalGuard -- "Row Lock" --> TableRO
    FinalGuard --> DBWriter
    
    DBWriter -- "Writes Decision" --> TableVR
    DBWriter -- "Updates Status" --> TableRE
    DBWriter -- "If PROCEED, Handoff" --> TableOB
```

### Where is the outcome stored?
The definitive outcome of this module is **always** stored in the `ValidationResult` table in your Neon PostgreSQL database.

**Table: `ValidationResult`**
*   **`decision`**: Either `PROCEED` (worth recovering) or `STOP` (not worth it).
*   **`stopReason`**: If it stopped, it tells you exactly why (e.g., `ALREADY_RESOLVED`, `ACTIONABILITY_INSUFFICIENT`, `ECONOMICALLY_NOT_WORTHWHILE`).
*   **Metrics**: Stores the exact `actionabilityScore`, `netExpectedRecovery`, `diagnosedCause`, and `priority` used to make the decision.

**Table: `OutboxEvent`**
*   If the decision was `PROCEED`, the worker *also* inserts a row into `OutboxEvent` with `eventType: VALIDATION_COMPLETED`. This is how the next module (Intervention Selection) knows to start working.
